<h2>The break at 1950</h2>
<p>Names that peaked before 1950 were built differently. 215 of them are in the cohort, and 13 percent lost half their births inside a decade. The median one took 17 years.</p>
<p>The 446 names that peaked after 1950 went faster. 47 percent halved inside ten years. Median: 11 years.</p>
<p>The survivor split is starker. 20 percent of the prewar names were still above half their peak 30 years later. Since 1950, 3 percent were.</p>
