<p>A girl born in 1987 grew up in a country that had already decided against her name. By second grade, the supply of Jessicas had been cut in half.</p>
<p>Her mother''s generation had a slower deal. <a href="/name/Jennifer/">Jennifer</a> peaked at 63600 in 1972 and took 16 years to halve. Same country, same schools, nearly twice the runway.</p>
<h2>Men hold longer</h2>
<p>414 of the 661 names belong to girls. 247 to boys.</p>
<p>98 percent of the girls'' names halved inside 30 years. 81 percent of the boys'' names did. Median half-life: 11 years for girls, 16 for boys.</p>
<p>Boys are named for grandfathers, saints, and fathers. The name is an inheritance, and an inheritance resists revision. Girls are named for the moment. Moments end.</p>
