<h2>The ones that held</h2>
<p>Only 7 names that peaked above 10,000 births after 1950 never halved inside 30 years. 6 of them are boys'' names.</p>
<p><a href="/name/Michael/">Michael</a> is the largest. 92781 boys in 1957. In 1987, 30 years on, it was still at 63664.</p>
<p><a href="/name/Mary/">Mary</a> peaked at 73984 in 1921 and was still at 65721 in 1951. <a href="/name/Joseph/">Joseph</a> peaked at 32749 in 1956 and was at 28834 in 1986. Both are liturgical names, which is a kind of long-term storage.</p>
